`Use size-based chunking with overlap for both, since uniform chunk sizes simplify the retrieval pipeline.`,
`Skip chunking and place every retrieved document in full into the context window for each query.`], correct:1, rationale:`Structure-based chunking exploits guaranteed formatting when it exists; size-based chunking with overlap is the reliable fallback when it doesn't.`},
{domain:4, official:false, fromCourse:true, q:`After splitting a long report into chunks, retrieval quality drops because individual chunks lose their connection to the surrounding document (e.g., a chunk about "results" doesn't indicate which experiment it refers to). What technique addresses this?`, options:[
`Increase the number of retrieved chunks returned for each query significantly, in order to compensate for this.`,
