`Switch entirely away from vector search, toward BM25 lexical keyword search instead.`,
`Remove all chunk boundaries entirely, and embed the full document as a single vector.`], correct:1, rationale:`Contextual retrieval re-attaches document-level context to each chunk before embedding, restoring the ties that plain chunking strips away.`},
{domain:1, official:false, q:`Your document-analysis agent begins every session with 6-8 exploratory tool calls just to discover which reports exist in the knowledge base before it can answer anything. What MCP design change removes this overhead?`, options:[
`Expose the report catalog as an MCP resource, so the available documents are visible up front without exploratory tool calls.`,
`Add a search_reports tool with a much more detailed description so the agent finds documents in fewer calls.`,
`Cache the agent's first exploration results in CLAUDE.md so later sessions can skip the discovery phase.`,
`Hardcode the current list of report names into the system prompt and update it whenever reports change.`], correct:0, rationale:`MCP resources exist precisely to expose content catalogs (document lists, schemas, hierarchies), giving agents visibility into available data without spending tool calls on discovery. A search tool still costs exploratory calls; hardcoded lists go stale.`},
{domain:1, official:false, q:`Your team needs Claude Code to interact with Jira for standard issue tracking (create, read, transition issues). An engineer proposes writing a custom MCP server for full control. What should you recommend?`, options:[
`Use an existing community MCP server for Jira, and reserve custom server development for workflows specific to your team.`,
