`Add a pre-processing routing classifier that picks the correct tool before the model ever sees the request.`,
`Merge both tools into a single analyze_anything tool so misrouting becomes structurally impossible.`], correct:[0,1], rationale:`The blueprint lists both remedies: differentiated naming/descriptions with boundaries, and auditing the system prompt for keyword-sensitive wording that can override well-written descriptions. A routing layer bypasses the model's language understanding; merging produces one overloaded tool with an unclear contract.`},
{domain:1, official:false, q:`You added a powerful MCP semantic code-search server, but logs show Claude Code keeps using built-in Grep instead, producing worse results on conceptual queries. What is the recommended fix?`, options:[
`Enhance the MCP tool's description to explain in detail its capabilities and outputs, so the model can tell when it beats built-in Grep.`,
