`The extraction schema is too strict; loosening the validation rules will let the retries pass.`,
`The retries need a higher temperature so the model explores alternative readings of the document.`], correct:0, rationale:`Retries with error feedback fix format and structural errors; they cannot conjure information absent from the source. Appending the validation error is the right move for correctable failures — this is not one of them.`},
{domain:3, official:false, q:`Compliance documents arrive continuously and must each be processed within 30 hours of arrival. You want the Message Batches API for its 50% savings, knowing a batch may take up to 24 hours. What submission strategy meets the SLA?`, options:[
`Submit batches on a fixed schedule every 4 hours, keeping worst-case wait plus 24-hour processing within the 30-hour SLA.`,
`Submit batches every 8 hours — three submissions per day is comfortably frequent for a 30-hour SLA.`,
`Submit each document as its own single-item batch immediately on arrival, to minimize waiting time.`,
`Submit one batch daily and mark it high priority, which guarantees completion within the SLA window.`], correct:0, rationale:`A document arriving just after a submission waits up to one full interval before its batch starts: interval + 24h must stay within 30h, so 4-hour windows work (28h worst case) while 8-hour windows can breach it (32h). Per-document batches forfeit throughput benefits; the Batches API has no priority flag and no latency SLA.`},
{domain:3, official:false, q:`Your CI review bot labels findings as critical/major/minor, but identical issues receive different severities across runs and developers are losing trust. What most reliably improves consistency?`, options:[
`Define explicit criteria for each severity level, with a concrete code example illustrating each level, directly in the prompt.`,
`Add an instruction telling the model to "assign severities consistently and conservatively."`,
`Run three review passes per finding and take the majority-vote severity as the final label.`,
`Have the model attach a confidence score to each severity so low-confidence labels can be filtered out.`], correct:0, rationale:`Explicit severity criteria with concrete examples per level is the blueprint's remedy for inconsistent classification. Vague adverbs like "consistently" do not improve precision; majority voting triples cost and hides the root cause; self-reported confidence is poorly calibrated.`},
{domain:3, official:false, q:`Your support agent handles clear-cut requests well but behaves erratically on ambiguous ones (e.g., "my order is wrong" — replacement? refund? escalation?). Detailed prose instructions have not helped. What is the recommended technique?`, options:[
`Add 2-4 targeted few-shot examples of ambiguous requests, each showing the reasoning for why one action was chosen over the plausible alternatives.`,
