`Route ambiguous requests to a separate classification model before the main agent sees them.`,
`Instruct the agent to ask a clarifying question whenever it detects any ambiguity in the request.`], correct:0, rationale:`A small set of targeted examples that demonstrate reasoning on ambiguous cases lets the model generalize judgment to novel patterns. Bulk examples add token cost without teaching the decision boundary; always-asking degrades the experience on requests the agent could resolve.`},
{domain:3, official:false, multi:true, q:`Documents in your extraction pipeline sometimes lack a value for certain schema fields, or contain values that fit no predefined category. Which TWO schema-design choices prevent the model from fabricating data in these cases?`, options:[
`Make fields optional/nullable when source documents may legitimately not contain the information.`,
