`That the model's average confidence score is at or above 97%, matching the measured accuracy figure.`,
`That a reprocessing fallback exists for any document a user later flags as incorrectly extracted.`], correct:0, rationale:`Aggregate accuracy can hide systematically poor performance on specific document types or fields. The blueprint requires validating accuracy by segment before automating high-confidence extractions. Sample size does not address segment blindness; average confidence says nothing about per-segment calibration.`},
{domain:4, official:false, multi:true, q:`You automated high-confidence extractions and route only low-confidence ones to humans. Which TWO ongoing practices keep this arrangement safe over time?`, options:[
`Stratified random sampling of high-confidence extractions, to measure their true error rate and detect novel error patterns.`,
