`Progressively raising the automation threshold as volume grows, to keep the human review workload constant.`,
`Re-running each high-confidence extraction twice and auto-accepting whenever both runs agree.`], correct:[0,1], rationale:`The blueprint prescribes stratified sampling of high-confidence outputs (ongoing error measurement, novel pattern detection) and calibrating confidence thresholds on labeled sets. Raising thresholds for workload reasons decouples automation from accuracy; run-to-run agreement measures stability, not correctness.`},
{domain:4, official:false, q:`Two credible sources give different figures for the same statistic — a 2023 industry report says 34%, a 2025 academic study says 41%. Your document-analysis subagent must pass findings onward. What should it do?`, options:[
`Include both values, annotated with source attribution and publication dates, and let the coordinator decide how to reconcile them before synthesis.`,
`Report the 41% figure, since the more recent study supersedes the older industry report.`,
`Report the average of the two figures (37.5%), citing both sources as joint support for the estimate.`,
`Report the academic figure, since peer-reviewed sources outrank industry reports in credibility.`], correct:0, rationale:`Conflicting statistics from credible sources should be preserved and annotated with attribution and dates — not resolved by recency or authority heuristics, which discard information. The two figures may measure different populations or timeframes; publication dates prevent temporal differences from being misread as contradictions.`},
{domain:0, official:false, q:`Your agentic loop calls the API, then decides whether to keep going. Which condition should drive the decision to execute tools and iterate again?`, options:[
`The response carries stop_reason "tool_use", so you execute the requested tools and send their results back for the next iteration.`,
`The response text contains a phrase such as "let me check that", which signals the model intends to use a tool.`,
`A fixed iteration counter has not yet reached its cap, so another turn is allowed.`,
`The response contains no text block, which indicates the model is still working rather than answering.`], correct:0, rationale:`The loop is driven by stop_reason: continue on "tool_use", terminate on "end_turn". Parsing natural language signals, relying on an iteration cap as the primary stopping mechanism, or inspecting text presence are the three anti-patterns the blueprint names explicitly.`},
{domain:0, official:false, q:`After executing the tools Claude requested, what must happen before the next API call for the loop to work correctly?`, options:[
`The tool results are appended to the conversation history so the model can reason about them when choosing the next action.`,
