`The conversation is reset and only the original user request plus the final tool result are sent.`,
`The tool results are stored server-side and referenced by identifier, since the model retains them between calls.`], correct:0, rationale:`Tool results must be added to the conversation as messages: that is how the model incorporates new information into its reasoning. The model retains nothing between requests, so resetting or referencing results externally breaks the loop.`},
{domain:0, official:false, q:`You add an iteration cap of 10 to your agentic loop as a safety net. A reviewer objects to how you are using it. What is the legitimate role of that cap?`, options:[
`A backstop against runaway loops, while stop_reason remains the actual termination signal.`,
