`A cost control that should be tuned down until most tasks finish exactly at the cap.`,
`A signal to the model, passed in the system prompt, telling it how many tools it may call.`], correct:0, rationale:`An arbitrary iteration cap as the primary stopping mechanism is a named anti-pattern. It is acceptable only as a backstop; correct termination comes from stop_reason "end_turn".`},
{domain:0, official:false, q:`You spent a long session mapping a legacy payment module with Claude Code. Two days later the team merged a refactor of that module and you want to continue the investigation. What is the most reliable approach?`, options:[
`Start a fresh session with a structured summary of the prior findings, since the earlier tool results no longer reflect the code on disk.`,
