`Few-shot examples showing several above-threshold refunds being escalated.`,
`A post-hoc audit job that flags refunds above 500 dollars for reversal the next day.`], correct:0, rationale:`When a business rule requires guaranteed compliance, hooks give a deterministic block; prompt instructions and few-shot examples have a non-zero failure rate. A next-day audit accepts the violation rather than preventing it.`},
{domain:0, official:false, multi:true, q:`Your coordinator delegates to four subagents. Which TWO practices follow the blueprint for context passing?`, options:[
`Include the complete findings from prior agents directly in the synthesis subagent's prompt.`,
`Use structured formats that separate content from metadata such as source URLs and page numbers.`,
`Rely on the subagent inheriting the coordinator's conversation history automatically.`,
`Store findings in a shared memory the subagents read at spawn time without being told about it.`], correct:[0,1], rationale:`Subagents operate with isolated context: nothing is inherited automatically and nothing is shared implicitly between invocations. Context must be provided explicitly in the prompt, and structured formats preserve attribution through the handoff.`},
{domain:1, official:false, q:`A single analyze_document tool is used for summarising, pulling out data points, and comparing versions. The agent frequently returns the wrong shape of output. What is the appropriate remedy?`, options:[
`Split it into purpose-specific tools such as extract_data_points, summarize_content and compare_versions, each with a defined input and output contract.`,
`Keep one tool and add a mode parameter with an enum of the three behaviours.`,
`Keep one tool and describe the three behaviours in detail in the system prompt instead.`,
`Have the agent call the tool twice and pick whichever output looks better.`], correct:0, rationale:`Generic overloaded tools produce unreliable selection and unclear contracts. The blueprint prescribes splitting them into purpose-specific tools with defined input and output contracts.`},
{domain:1, official:false, q:`Your tool descriptions are detailed and well differentiated, yet the agent still routes document questions to the web search tool. The system prompt tells it to "search for relevant information before answering". What should you investigate first?`, options:[
`The system prompt wording, since keyword-sensitive instructions can create unintended tool associations that override good descriptions.`,
`The order of the tools in the tools array, since the model favours the first entries.`,
`The temperature setting, since lower values make tool selection more deterministic.`,
